{"kind":"request","text":"Security R4 and R13 (6dd06d03 sections 1.4, 2.4 and 5): tokens.\n\nWork:\n1. R4. A /site read reuses one Artifacts read token for each repository and ref while the token lives, instead of a mint and a revoke for each request (packages/scope/src/site/host.ts:181-205).\n2. R4. Site reads have a per-address window. A read above it answers 429.\n3. R13. The plaintext of an unread read token is deleted at the token's end (credential-store.ts:172-212).\n4. R13. A member holds at most a bounded number of open read tokens. A mint above the bound is refused `limit`. `destination.read-token` keeps its 24-hour lifetime.\n\nWitnesses: N site reads of one ref mint one token; the read above the window answers 429; an unread token's plaintext is gone after its end; the member's token above the bound is refused.\n\nCloses 1.4 and the read-token half of 2.4.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 7 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Token reuse and address window for /site; sweep of unread tokens; per-member open-token bound; closes 1.4, 2.4 read tokens. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}